Mor ke pankhe. The national bird of India is associated with many Hindu gods, spoken of in folktales, drawn in many paintings and is one of the many things that represent India. The beautiful bird that brings awe to many people and is not only mentioned in Hindu culture, but as well as Christianity. My trip to India this year was so amazing because I saw a peacock actually lift its tail and dance! Growing up my mom would tell me the many stories of how peacocks would gather around her home when she was young and leave thousands of feathers behind. She would keep the feathers in her home, which is believed to bring good luck in the home. I wish I could’ve gotten a video of the mor dancing, but I was too captivated by the graciousness of this beautiful bird. I also wish I could’ve found a real peacock feather to keep in my home. However, after the dance, the feathers slowly fell down and it disappeared into the forest. This will not be my last inspirational post by peacocks, it took me forever to narrow down what look I wanted to go for and I will share all the ideas I had with you slowly. 
___
